# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Zola build output
/site/public

# Fuzzing: the targets and the seeder are committed, the corpus and artifacts are generated
# (`cargo run -p xtask -- fuzz-corpus`) and the build output is enormous.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/

.DS_Store

# ── Internal notes, feature specifications and third-party sources ─────────────

# Architecture notes (not published): the D/R-numbered decisions and risks, the
# errata, and ROADMAP.md, the spec of specs — every open item names its feature
# specification.
#
# The OCPI specification corpus — the pinned checkouts of github.com/ocpi/ocpi
# that `cargo run -p xtask -- spec-sync --fetch` materialises, and the release
# PDFs — lives at `concepts/reference/` and is covered by this line: CC BY-ND 4.0
# and not redistributed. What is committed is spec-sources.toml and its lock.
# `$OCPI_REFERENCE` points the xtask elsewhere.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that
# produces them: one `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item (spec, plan, research,
# tasks, threat model), `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, and the `/speckit-*`
# skills. Same rule as `concepts/` — internal, and the published tree may not
# cite a path its reader does not have; `scripts/concepts-check.sh` fails on one
# that does.
#
# Until 2026-11-20 `specs/` held the OCPI corpus now under `concepts/reference/`;
# a stale copy is ignored by the same line. Matches ocpp-kit, eebus and metering.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
